{"id": "93b76207-a2f7-4388-934d-b865496b2f7c", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T16:03:17.315884", "source": "agent", "parent_id": null, "system_prompt": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Collaborate with the researcher to develop an experiment design for the original task. First inspect the masked repository and supplied inputs, then use end_researcher_turn with stage=plan to propose an approach, consequential choices and uncertainties. Wait for explicit researcher approval before developing the full design. After approval, hand off stage=result with the complete design in answer, supported by rationale, controls, feasible checks and repository observations in evidence. State assumptions separately from fixed task requirements. No executed experiment or invented outcome is required for this design-only task. Use inspect_repository and execute_check for exploration. Share concrete findings: private tool output is not automatically sent to the researcher. Revise when needed; do not invent objections or ambiguities to extend the conversation. The researcher decides when to stop."}, "tools": [{"description": "List a repository directory or read a text file. Paths are relative to the task workspace.", "action_type": "InspectRepositoryAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "InspectRepositoryTool", "title": "inspect_repository"}, {"description": "Run a shell command in the isolated task workspace. Use small exploratory checks before submitting your plan.", "action_type": "ExecuteCheckAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ExecuteCheckTool", "title": "execute_check"}, {"description": "Yield a proposed approach (stage=plan) or completed experiment design (stage=result), with evidence, assumptions and uncertainties. The researcher decides when to finish.", "action_type": "ReviewHandoffAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ReviewHandoffTool", "title": "end_researcher_turn"}], "dynamic_context": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "<CURRENT_DATETIME>\nThe current date and time is: 2026-10-22T16:02\n</CURRENT_DATETIME>"}, "kind": "SystemPromptEvent"}
{"id": "bb8cf6ec-d461-42b2-8396-bcaf4f99c9a5", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T16:03:17.317681", "source": "user", "parent_id": "93b76207-a2f7-4388-934d-b865496b2f7c", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Hola. Antes de pedir el diseño completo, quiero solo inspección + propuesta de enfoque, nada de solución todavía.\\n\\n1) Inspección de insumos: revisa /workspace y confirma qué hay realmente (código, datos, checkpoints, papers locales). En track.md dice que es tarea de diseño y que no se requieren repositorio ni cómputo; verifica eso con comandos ligeros y reporta qué existe y qué no. No inventes datasets ni resultados.\\n\\n2) Propuesta de enfoque (solo el esqueleto, con justificación breve):\\n   - Pregunta operativa: ¿el loop de feedback químico (p-logP, QED, afinidad de unión) mejora propiedad molecular SIN distorsionar la distribución estructural real?\\n   - Brazos a comparar: (a) generador base sin feedback, (b) feedback solo propiedades, (c) feedback propiedades + término anti-alucinación/validador, (d) feedback con penalización de modo/cadena (p. ej. castigo a colas de carbono ultra-largas y duplicados Near-Unmatched). Deja claro qué variables son fijas y cuáles son tus supuestos.\\n   - Métricas de propiedad: QED, logP/p-logP, SA, MW, y un score de docking/scoring si aplica (declara el receptor y la herramienta como supuesto).\\n   - Métricas de diversidad y alineación distribucional: interno vs externo (Self/External similarity), Scaffold Network / número de scaffolds únicos, FCD o similar, Distribution of Chain Length (DoF de cadenas, Longest Chain, % moléculas con cadena > umbral), Murcko frameworks únicos, validez/sancibilidad y tasa de \\\"molecular hallucination\\\" definida operacionalmente.\\n   - Controles esenciales que quiero ver nombrados: semilla y repetición (n>=3), mismo presupuesto de muestras y pasos de entrenamiento, control de temperatura/muestreo, control de overfitting al reward (reward hacking), y un control que use puntuación por proxy (p. ej. QED solo) para separar ganancia real de sobreajuste al scorer.\\n   - Análisis plan: test por brazo con corrección múltiple, intervalos de confianza, análisis de trade-off propiedad vs diversidad (curvas Pareto), y desglose por longitud de cadena para probar el efecto de \\\"ultra-long carbon chains\\\".\\n\\n3) Supuestos e incertidumbres que debes declarar explícitamente: qué generador/modelo base se asume, qué datos de entrenamiento se asumen, si hay receptor/diana real o es sintético, presupuesto de cómputo, y qué se reporta como supuesto versus elección fijada.\\n\\nEntrega ahora: (i) hallazgos de inspección, (ii) enfoque propuesto en bullets, (iii) lista de supuestos/incertidumbres, (iv) qué necesitarías de mí. No produzcas todavía el diseño final ni métricas simuladas.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Incorporating the chemical feedback mechanism, which leverages properties such as p-logP, QED, and binding affinity, directly improves the generation of molecules with superior chemical properties and reduces molecular hallucinations in targeted molecule discovery tasks. Does embedding this feedback loop better align molecule generation with real-world distributions, preserving structural diversity (e.g., avoiding over-representation of ultra-long carbon chains) while enhancing property scores?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
